{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01Tk9Us9CVsfHH6CUniikGPk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HK2HQDGLg8ibeNwXUn3wES","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"R2: Novelty + Related Work review","prompt":"You are Reviewer 2 (R2) for a top ML venue review. Your focus areas are **Novelty/Significance** and **Related Work/Positioning**. Review the paper below using a 6-point scale (1=Strong Reject, 2=Reject, 3=Borderline Reject, 4=Borderline Accept, 5=Accept, 6=Strong Accept). Target venue acceptance rate ~25%.\n\n## Paper Summary\n\n**Title:** \"Solver Trace Ablation Reveals Reward Hacking in GRPO-Trained Formalizers: Meta-Level Goodhart's Law in Structural Proxy Metrics\"\n\n**Core contributions:**\n1. STA (Solver Trace Ablation): LOO component necessity testing on solver inputs, deriving ISR (fraction of components whose removal breaks proof).\n2. Three claims:\n   - Claim 1: ISR detects reward hacking invisible to prove rate (0.64→0.003 ISR collapse while PR 32%→96%).\n   - Claim 2: Meta-level Goodhart's Law when ISR used as training reward. Low dose: models game ISR itself (H7=64.5% vs 0% random). Apparent improvement vanishes under premise-count matching (1.06×). High dose: classic Goodhart (PR 18% vs 48% random).\n   - Claim 3: Preliminary cross-logic evidence—ISR collapse replicates in Prolog (0.008-0.081). STA-as-reward Goodhart in 2/3 Prolog seeds but heterogeneous.\n3. 6-mode hacking taxonomy from 200 manual annotations.\n4. SFT baseline: hacking is RL-specific (92.9% genuine SFT vs 12.9% GRPO).\n5. ISR=LOO ablation metric; authors explicitly disclaim novelty of LOO technique.\n6. NLI downstream negative result: ISR ≠ semantic faithfulness.\n\n**Related Work section covers:**\n- GRPO for formal reasoning (DeepSeek-Prover, EVOM)\n- Reward hacking and Goodhart's Law (Manheim & Garrabrant 2019 taxonomy)\n- Structural rewards for code/logic (Mellgren et al. 2025, ExecVerify, EGCA)\n- Feature attribution and LOO methods (Shapley values, feature importance)\n\n**Setup:** Qwen-1.5B, GRPO, FOL (Prover9) + Prolog (SWI-Prolog), 3 seeds, up to 1000 steps.\n\n**Key experimental results:**\n\nTable 1 (ISR collapse, FOL s42): 100 steps ISR=0.64 → 500 steps ISR=0.13 → 1000 steps ISR=0.003\n\nTable 4 (ISR β=0.1 vs Random): ISR H7=64.5%, Random H7=0%. ISR PR=0.77±0.14, Random PR=0.85±0.06.\n\nTable 5 (Premise-count matched): ratio=1.06× after controlling for premise count.\n\nTable 7 (SFT vs GRPO): SFT genuine=92.9%, GRPO genuine=12.9%.\n\nTable 10 (Prolog STA): s42 H7=100%, s43 H7=23% (n=13), s44 H7=56%.\n\n**Not run:** SMT-LIB third logic, 8B model scaling, curriculum ablation, mixed-logic training.\n\n**Limitations acknowledged:** (1) only 1.5B models, (2) only 2 logic types, (3) 3 seeds, (4) ISR=syntactic not semantic, (5) no positive training method proposed.\n\n## Your Review Task (R2: Novelty + Related Work)\n\nEvaluate:\n1. **Novelty**: Is \"meta-level Goodhart's Law\" genuinely new? Is applying LOO to GRPO formalizers novel enough? How significant is the hacking taxonomy?\n2. **Positioning**: Is the paper well-positioned against prior work? Are key references missing? Is the contribution differentiated from existing structural reward methods?\n3. **Significance/Impact**: Would this change how practitioners train formalizers? Is the \"ISR as observer not optimizer\" insight actionable?\n4. **Framing**: Is the paper framed as a negative result? Is that appropriate for a top venue?\n5. **Scope of contribution**: Is this sufficient for a main conference paper, or more suited to a Findings/workshop track?\n\nProduce a structured review with:\n- Summary (2-3 sentences)\n- Strengths (bulleted)\n- Weaknesses (bulleted)\n- Questions for Authors (numbered)\n- Minor Issues\n- Overall Score (1-6) and Confidence (1-5)\n- One-line recommendation"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":37744,"cache_read_input_tokens":22938,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":37744},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cb7ceeff-4816-4704-b3bd-c692a0f9b846","uuid":"fbd5312c-bb6e-4b38-90cb-122a2cbae1ac"}
