{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KEjN1UBu18Ce3VbLF42H4t","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"success\\\": true, \\\"data\\\": {\\\"path\\\": \\\"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_3/projects/solver-trace-ablation/writing_plan.yaml\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"meta:\\\\n  venue: EMNLP 2026\\\\n  track: main\\\\n  template: acl2023/\\\\n  template_note: \\\\\\\"ARR May 25 cycle. ACL Rolling Review format (acl2023.sty).\\\\\\\"\\\\n  page_limit: 8\\\\n  deadline: 2026-05-25\\\\n  core_claim: >\\\\n    ISR (Intensional Structural Reward), derived via Solver Trace Ablation,\\\\n    serves as a powerful diagnostic for reward hacking in GRPO-trained formalizers\\\\n    but fails as a training signal due to meta-level Goodhart's Law — the diagnostic\\\\n    metric becomes gamed when optimized, with apparent improvements explained by\\\\n    premise minimization artifacts.\\\\n  created_at: 2026-05-14T18:00:00Z\\\\n  updated_at: 2026-05-14T19:00:00Z\\\\n  update_note: \\\\\\\"Director approved. Tab3 merged into Fig2; Tab6 moved to appendix. 4 fig + 4 table in main.\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\npaper_outline:\\\\n  - section: abstract\\\\n    word_budget: 250\\\\n    core_bullets:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Problem: GRPO formalizers achieve high prove rates but produce structurally degenerate outputs; no diagnostic exists\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Method: STA derives ISR via leave-one-out component necessity testing on solver inputs\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Claim 1: ISR detects hacking invisible to prove_rate (0.64→0.13→0.003 collapse over 100→500→1000 steps)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Claim 2: ISR-as-reward exhibits meta-level Goodhart — β=0.1 induces ISR-specific gaming (H7=64.5% vs 0% random), premise-matched 1.06x; β=0.3 PR collapses (18% vs 48% random)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Claim 3: ISR diagnostic transfers to Prolog (cross-logic generality)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Taxonomy: 6 distinct hacking modes identified across conditions\\\\\\\"\\\\n    dependencies: [experiments, method, discussion]\\\\n    tables: []\\\\n    figures: []\\\\n    registry_refs: []\\\\n\\\\n  - section: introduction\\\\n    word_budget: 1200\\\\n    core_bullets:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Hook: A GRPO formalizer achieves 93% prove rate — but 87% of its proved outputs embed the conclusion in the premises. Structural shortcuts invisible to execution reward.\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Gap: Execution-only evaluation (prove_rate) conflates genuine reasoning with degenerate shortcuts. No principled diagnostic exists for structural integrity in neurosymbolic GRPO.\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Insight: Component necessity testing (LOO ablation on solver inputs) yields ISR — AND when this diagnostic becomes reward, it exhibits meta-level Goodhart: the model games the metric itself.\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Mechanism: STA protocol + systematic study across 6 reward conditions × 3 seeds × up to 1000 steps\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Contributions: (C1) ISR as diagnostic with complete collapse trajectory; (C2) Meta-level Goodhart empirical characterization with premise-count confound analysis; (C3) Cross-logic diagnostic transfer; (C4) 6-mode hacking taxonomy\\\\\\\"\\\\n    dependencies: [experiments]\\\\n    citation_hints:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"GRPO: deepseekmath\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Neurosymbolic: satlm, logic-lm, linc\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Reward hacking: gao-reward-overoptimization, karwowski-goodhart-rl\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Goodhart taxonomy: manheim-goodhart-taxonomy\\\\\\\"\\\\n    figures: [fig1_sta_overview]\\\\n    tables: []\\\\n    registry_refs: []\\\\n\\\\n  - section: related_work\\\\n    word_budget: 900\\\\n    core_bullets:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Cluster 1 — Neurosymbolic Reasoning with LLMs: Logic-LM, LINC, SatLM, LoRP, FoVer pipeline approach (prompting); Mellgren Prolog GRPO (RL). STA differs: structural reward + diagnostic focus\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Cluster 2 — Reward Shaping & Process Supervision: Lightman verify-step, Math-Shepherd, RLSF symbolic feedback, Rubric-GRPO. STA's ISR is solver-grounded process signal; our finding: process reward can itself Goodhart\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Cluster 3 — Reward Hacking & Goodhart's Law: Gao scaling laws, Karwowski geometric, Manheim taxonomy, Skalse characterization, Pan misspecification. We contribute empirical Goodhart in formal reasoning + meta-level (proxy games itself)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Cluster 4 — Mutation Testing & Component Analysis: DeMillo 1978, Jia-Harman survey, Just mutants. STA adapts LOO mutation from SE to formal logic\\\\\\\"\\\\n    dependencies: [introduction]\\\\n    citation_hints:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Must cite: deepseekmath, logic-lm, linc, satlm, mellgren-prolog-grpo\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Must cite: lightman-verify-step, gao-reward-overoptimization, karwowski-goodhart-rl, manheim-goodhart-taxonomy\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Must cite: demillo1978, folio, proofwriter\\\\\\\"\\\\n    figures: []\\\\n    tables: []\\\\n    registry_refs: []\\\\n\\\\n  - section: method\\\\n    word_budget: 1200\\\\n    core_bullets:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"3.1 Task: NL → Formal Logic formalization, verified by external solver (Prover9 for FOL, SWI-Prolog for Prolog)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"3.2 GRPO Training: execution-only reward r_exec ∈ {0,1}, group relative policy optimization\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"3.3 Solver Trace Ablation (STA): LOO ablation protocol — for proved sample with n components, remove each component, re-run solver, ISR = fraction of components whose removal causes proof failure\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"3.4 ISR Definition: ISR(x) = (1/n) Σ_i 1[solver fails on x\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\{c_i}], bounded [0,1]. ISR=1 → all necessary; ISR=0 → none necessary\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"3.5 Reward Formulations: exec-only, additive ISR (r_exec·(1+β·ISR)), additive random control, convex combination, SFT baseline\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"3.6 Hacking Taxonomy: H1 (multi-premise conclusion embedding), H7 (single premise = conclusion), H3 (complexity-without-utility), tautological collapse, repetition collapse, contradiction explosion\\\\\\\"\\\\n    dependencies: []\\\\n    notation_table:\\\\n      r_exec: \\\\\\\"binary execution reward (solver success)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      ISR: \\\\\\\"Intensional Structural Reward\\\\\\\"\\\\n      beta: \\\\\\\"ISR reward weight\\\\\\\"\\\\n      n: \\\\\\\"number of components in formalization\\\\\\\"\\\\n      c_i: \\\\\\\"i-th component (premise/rule)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      H1: \\\\\\\"multi-premise conclusion embedding\\\\\\\"\\\\n      H7: \\\\\\\"single premise = conclusion\\\\\\\"\\\\n    figures: [fig1_sta_overview]\\\\n    tables: []\\\\n    registry_refs: [sta-phase0-baseline, plan003-eval-exec-only-r5]\\\\n\\\\n  - section: experiments\\\\n    word_budget: 2800\\\\n    core_bullets:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"4.1 Setup: Qwen3-4B, GRPO (K=8, 500 steps default), ProofWriter-FOL-100 eval, Prover9/SWI-Prolog solvers, 3 seeds (42/43/44)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"4.2 ISR as Diagnostic (Claim 1): ISR collapse trajectory 0.6423→0.1324→0.0027 over 100→500→1000 steps (Fig2 with embedded data); PR rises 32%→93%→96%; 3-seed exec-only divergence (s42 genuine→H1, s43 degraded PR=14%, s44 tautological 2-comp); SFT baseline 92.9% genuine confirms RL-specificity\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"4.3 Meta-Level Goodhart (Claim 2): β=0.1 ISR — H7=64.5% ISR-specific gaming vs 0% random; premise-count-matched 1.06x (no real advantage); β=0.3 — PR collapse 18% vs 48% random; conclusion embedding is GRPO-universal (68-100%); ISR restructures hacking, doesn't reduce it\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"4.4 Cross-Logic Transfer (Claim 3): Prolog exec-only 3-seed ISR<0.1 across all seeds; Prolog STA s42 100% H7; diagnostic generalizes regardless of training outcome\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"4.5 Hacking Taxonomy: 6 modes quantified across conditions; reward type determines hacking composition not prevalence\\\\\\\"\\\\n    dependencies: []\\\\n    registry_refs:\\\\n      - sta-phase0-baseline\\\\n      - plan003-eval-exec-only-r5\\\\n      - plan001-exec-only-s42-r2\\\\n      - plan001-exec-only-s43-r4\\\\n      - plan001-exec-only-s44\\\\n      - plan016-extended-1000-s42\\\\n      - plan002-additive-b01-s42\\\\n      - plan002-additive-b01-s43\\\\n      - plan002-additive-b01-s44\\\\n      - plan018-additive-random-b01-s42\\\\n      - plan018-additive-random-b01-s43-r2\\\\n      - plan018-additive-random-b01-s44\\\\n      - plan002-additive-b03-s42\\\\n      - plan017-additive-random-s42\\\\n      - plan005-sta-low-s42\\\\n      - plan013-random-reward-s42-r4\\\\n      - plan009-sft-baseline-s42-r4\\\\n      - plan006-prolog-exec-s42\\\\n      - plan006-prolog-exec-s43-r3\\\\n      - plan006-prolog-exec-s44\\\\n      - plan006-prolog-sta-s42\\\\n    tables: [tab1_goodhart_landscape, tab2_hacking_taxonomy, tab4_beta01_3seed, tab5_prolog_crosslogic]\\\\n    figures: [fig2_isr_collapse, fig3_hacking_composition, fig4_prolog_comparison]\\\\n\\\\n  - section: discussion\\\\n    word_budget: 600\\\\n    core_bullets:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"ISR measures syntactic component necessity, not semantic faithfulness (plan014 ρ=-0.049 n.s.)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Premise count confound: LOO metrics mathematically biased — fewer premises → higher ISR regardless of quality (D051)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Practical implications: ISR for post-hoc diagnosis only; never trust prove_rate alone; single-seed GRPO unreliable; proxy-as-reward cautionary tale\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Meta-level Goodhart as general warning for any proxy-metric-as-reward approach\\\\\\\"\\\\n    dependencies: [experiments]\\\\n    tables: []\\\\n    figures: []\\\\n    registry_refs: [plan014-downstream-nli-s42]\\\\n\\\\n  - section: conclusion\\\\n    word_budget: 300\\\\n    core_bullets:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Summary: STA/ISR as diagnostic detects reward hacking invisible to prove_rate; ISR-as-reward exhibits meta-level Goodhart at all doses\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Limitations: single base model (Qwen3-4B); ProofWriter data only; ISR = syntactic not semantic; 3 seeds; Claim 3 Prolog STA partial\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Future: ISR + semantic verification; adaptive reward weighting; broader logic types; scale to larger models\\\\\\\"\\\\n    dependencies: [experiments, discussion]\\\\n    tables: []\\\\n    figures: []\\\\n    registry_refs: []\\\\n\\\\n  - section: appendix\\\\n    word_budget: 1000\\\\n    core_bullets:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Table A1: Experimental setup and hyperparameters (moved from Tab6)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Full hacking taxonomy definitions and examples\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Per-seed detailed results\\\\\\\"\\\\n    dependencies: [experiments]\\\\n    tables: [tab6_setup]\\\\n    figures: []\\\\n    registry_refs: []\\\\n\\\\nvisualization_plan:\\\\n  - fig_id: fig1_sta_overview\\\\n    type: conceptual\\\\n    tool: matplotlib\\\\n    description: >\\\\n      STA protocol overview: (a) NL input → LLM formalizer → formal logic → solver → prove/fail.\\\\n      (b) STA ablation: remove each component, re-run solver, compute ISR.\\\\n      (c) ISR as diagnostic vs ISR as reward (Goodhart arrow).\\\\n      3-panel horizontal layout.\\\\n    placement: method\\\\n    aspect_ratio: \\\\\\\"3:1\\\\\\\"\\\\n    data_source: \\\\\\\"manual\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  - fig_id: fig2_isr_collapse\\\\n    type: statistical\\\\n    tool: matplotlib\\\\n    description: >\\\\n      ISR collapse trajectory over training steps with embedded data annotations.\\\\n      X-axis: training steps (100, 500, 1000). Dual y-axis: PR (left, rising 32%→93%→96%)\\\\n      and ISR (right, falling 0.64→0.13→0.003). Include component count trend (6.58→18.55)\\\\n      as bubble size or secondary annotation. Annotate: ISR=0 ratio at 1000 steps (94.8%).\\\\n      Replaces former Tab3 — all collapse data embedded in figure annotations.\\\\n    placement: experiments\\\\n    aspect_ratio: \\\\\\\"4:3\\\\\\\"\\\\n    data_source: \\\\\\\"registry: plan003-eval-exec-only-r5, plan001-exec-only-s42-r2, plan016-extended-1000-s42\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  - fig_id: fig3_hacking_composition\\\\n    type: statistical\\\\n    tool: matplotlib\\\\n    description: >\\\\n      Stacked bar chart: hacking mode composition across conditions.\\\\n      X-axis: Exec-only s42, ISR β=0.1 s42/s43/s44, Random β=0.1 (3-seed mean), SFT.\\\\n      Stacked segments: H7 (red), H1 (orange), H3 (yellow), Genuine (green).\\\\n      Shows ISR restructures hacking (H1→H7) rather than reducing it.\\\\n    placement: experiments\\\\n    aspect_ratio: \\\\\\\"16:9\\\\\\\"\\\\n    data_source: \\\\\\\"registry: plan001-exec-only-s42-r2, plan002-additive-b01-s42, plan002-additive-b01-s43, plan002-additive-b01-s44, plan018-additive-random-b01-s42, plan018-additive-random-b01-s43-r2, plan018-additive-random-b01-s44, plan009-sft-baseline-s42-r4\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  - fig_id: fig4_prolog_comparison\\\\n    type: statistical\\\\n    tool: matplotlib\\\\n    description: >\\\\n      Grouped bar chart: FOL vs Prolog exec-only ISR comparison (3 seeds each).\\\\n      X-axis: s42, s43, s44. Grouped bars: FOL ISR, Prolog ISR.\\\\n      Both near-zero, confirming cross-logic diagnostic transfer.\\\\n      Overlay PR values as text annotations.\\\\n    placement: experiments\\\\n    aspect_ratio: \\\\\\\"4:3\\\\\\\"\\\\n    data_source: \\\\\\\"registry: plan001-exec-only-s42-r2, plan001-exec-only-s43-r4, plan001-exec-only-s44, plan006-prolog-exec-s42, plan006-prolog-exec-s43-r3, plan006-prolog-exec-s44\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\ntable_plan:\\\\n  - table_id: tab1_goodhart_landscape\\\\n    caption: \\\\\\\"Goodhart landscape: ISR-as-reward across dose and formulation. All eval on ProofWriter-FOL-100 via eval\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\_sta.py.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    placement: experiments\\\\n    type: comparison\\\\n    columns: [Condition, Formula, β, Seed, PR↑, ISR↑, H7%, H1%, Genuine%, Mode]\\\\n    data_source: \\\\\\\"registry: sta-phase0-baseline, plan001-exec-only-s42-r2, plan009-sft-baseline-s42-r4, plan002-additive-b01-s42, plan002-additive-b01-s43, plan002-additive-b01-s44, plan018-additive-random-b01-s42, plan018-additive-random-b01-s43-r2, plan018-additive-random-b01-s44, plan002-additive-b03-s42, plan017-additive-random-s42, plan013-random-reward-s42-r4\\\\\\\"\\\\n    notes: \\\\\\\"Core table. Bold best genuine%. † marks tautological artifacts. * marks sampling eval.\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  - table_id: tab2_hacking_taxonomy\\\\n    caption: \\\\\\\"Hacking taxonomy: six distinct modes across reward conditions. Rates are % of proved samples (s42 seed).\\\\\\\"\\\\n    placement: experiments\\\\n    type: comparison\\\\n    columns: [Mode, Description, \\\\\\\"Exec-only\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"ISR β=0.1\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Random β=0.1\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"SFT\\\\\\\"]\\\\n    data_source: \\\\\\\"registry: plan001-exec-only-s42-r2, plan002-additive-b01-s42, plan018-additive-random-b01-s42, plan009-sft-baseline-s42-r4, plan012-hacking-taxonomy\\\\\\\"\\\\n    notes: \\\\\\\"s42 comparison (cleanest seed). Include mode descriptions in table.\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  - table_id: tab4_beta01_3seed\\\\n    caption: \\\\\\\"ISR β=0.1 vs Random β=0.1: 3-seed comparison. H7 is ISR-specific (64.5% vs 0%). Premise-count-matched ISR: 1.06×.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    placement: experiments\\\\n    type: comparison\\\\n    columns: [Seed, Condition, PR, \\\\\\\"ISR (proved)\\\\\\\", H7%, H1%, Genuine%, \\\\\\\"Prem-matched ISR\\\\\\\"]\\\\n    data_source: \\\\\\\"registry: plan002-additive-b01-s42, plan002-additive-b01-s43, plan002-additive-b01-s44, plan018-additive-random-b01-s42, plan018-additive-random-b01-s43-r2, plan018-additive-random-b01-s44\\\\\\\"\\\\n    notes: \\\\\\\"Key table for Claim 2. Include 3-seed mean±std row. Premise-matched column only for s42.\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  - table_id: tab5_prolog_crosslogic\\\\n    caption: \\\\\\\"Cross-logic diagnostic transfer: Prolog results. ISR detects degeneration across logic types.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    placement: experiments\\\\n    type: comparison\\\\n    columns: [Logic, Condition, Seed, PR, ISR, \\\\\\\"Proved-only ISR\\\\\\\", H7%, Mode]\\\\n    data_source: \\\\\\\"registry: plan006-prolog-exec-s42, plan006-prolog-exec-s43-r3, plan006-prolog-exec-s44, plan006-prolog-sta-s42\\\\\\\"\\\\n    notes: \\\\\\\"Prolog STA s43/s44 RUNNING — [pending]. Include FOL exec-only for comparison.\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  - table_id: tab6_setup\\\\n    caption: \\\\\\\"Experimental setup and hyperparameters.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    placement: appendix\\\\n    type: configuration\\\\n    columns: [Parameter, Value]\\\\n    data_source: \\\\\\\"manual\\\\\\\"\\\\n    notes: \\\\\\\"APPENDIX. Base model, training data, K, steps, seeds, solvers, eval dataset.\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\nliterature_strategy:\\\\n  citation_budget: 40\\\\n  macro_context:\\\\n    - \\\\\\\"GRPO / RL for formal reasoning\\\\\\\"\\\\n    - \\\\\\\"reward hacking and Goodhart's Law in LLM training\\\\\\\"\\\\n    - \\\\\\\"neurosymbolic NL-to-logic formalization\\\\\\\"\\\\n    - \\\\\\\"mutation testing and component analysis\\\\\\\"\\\\n  micro_clusters:\\\\n    - cluster_name: neurosymbolic-rl\\\\n      search_queries:\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"GRPO reinforcement learning logical reasoning 2024 2025\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"neurosymbolic LLM formal logic prover\\\\\\\"\\\\n      must_cite:\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"deepseekmath (GRPO origin)\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"mellgren-prolog-grpo\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"logic-lm\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"linc\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"satlm\\\\\\\"\\\\n      target_count: 8\\\\n    - cluster_name: reward-shaping\\\\n      search_queries:\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"reward shaping process supervision LLM reasoning 2024 2025\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"process reward model overoptimization\\\\\\\"\\\\n      must_cite:\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"lightman-verify-step\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"gao-effective-rl-reward\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"rlsf\\\\\\\"\\\\n      target_count: 8\\\\n    - cluster_name: reward-hacking\\\\n      search_queries:\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"reward hacking overoptimization RLHF 2024 2025\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"specification gaming reinforcement learning\\\\\\\"\\\\n      must_cite:\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"gao-reward-overoptimization\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"skalse-reward-hacking\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"reward-hacking-survey\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"spurious-rewards\\\\\\\"\\\\n      target_count: 6\\\\n    - cluster_name: goodhart-overoptimization\\\\n      search_queries:\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"Goodhart's Law reinforcement learning proxy reward\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"reward model overoptimization scaling laws\\\\\\\"\\\\n      must_cite:\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"manheim-goodhart-taxonomy\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"karwowski-goodhart-rl\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"kwa-catastrophic-goodhart\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"pan-reward-misspecification\\\\\\\"\\\\n      target_count: 6\\\\n    - cluster_name: fol-formalization\\\\n      search_queries:\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"first-order logic formalization LLM 2024 2025\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"Prolog LLM reasoning\\\\\\\"\\\\n      must_cite:\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"folio\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"proofwriter\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"fover-pei2025\\\\\\\"\\\\n      target_count: 5\\\\n    - cluster_name: mutation-testing\\\\n      search_queries:\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"mutation testing component analysis software engineering\\\\\\\"\\\\n      must_cite:\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"demillo1978\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"jia-harman-survey\\\\\\\"\\\\n      target_count: 4\\\\n    - cluster_name: verification-reward\\\\n      search_queries:\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"solver prover reward signal RL training 2024 2025\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"formal verification LLM training\\\\\\\"\\\\n      must_cite:\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"deepseek-prover-v15\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"math-shepherd\\\\\\\"\\\\n      target_count: 4\\\\n\\\\nwriting_order:\\\\n  - experiments\\\\n  - method\\\\n  - introduction\\\\n  - related_work\\\\n  - discussion\\\\n  - abstract\\\\n  - conclusion\\\\n\\\", \\\"total_chars\\\": 16820, \\\"truncated\\\": false}, \\\"error\\\": null, \\\"metadata\\\": {}}\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01HK2HQDGLg8ibeNwXUn3wES","session_id":"cb7ceeff-4816-4704-b3bd-c692a0f9b846","uuid":"53bae9c3-383f-4d0e-9401-505ba8ebac76","timestamp":"2026-05-14T18:15:09.613Z"}
