{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01U6qY6FGBRNLQk1ZnPZr1Ez","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Claim-Evidence Coverage Audit\n2\t\n3\t**Date**: 2026-05-14  \n4\t**Deadline**: 2026-05-25 (ARR May, 11 days remaining)  \n5\t**Registry snapshot**: 31 experiments (6 success, 9 negative, 14 failed, 2 running)\n6\t\n7\t---\n8\t\n9\t## Experiment Inventory (Paper-Usable)\n10\t\n11\t| ID | Condition | Formula | Steps | Seed | Eval Method | Status |\n12\t|----|-----------|---------|-------|------|-------------|--------|\n13\t| sta-phase0-baseline | Base model (no training) | — | 0 | — | inference | ✅ DONE |\n14\t| sta-gt-isr-baseline | Ground truth FOL | — | — | — | prover9 | ✅ DONE |\n15\t| plan003-eval-r5 | Exec-only early checkpoint | r = r_exec | 100 | 42 | eval_sta.py | ✅ DONE |\n16\t| plan001-s42-r2 | Exec-only | r = r_exec | 500 | 42 | eval_sta.py | ✅ DONE |\n17\t| plan001-s43-r4 | Exec-only | r = r_exec | 500 | 43 | **sampling only** | ⚠️ GAP |\n18\t| plan001-s44 | Exec-only | r = r_exec | 500 | 44 | eval_sta.py | ✅ DONE |\n19\t| plan005-sta-low | Convex ISR (α=0.9,β=0.1) | r = 0.9·r_exec + 0.1·r_exec·ISR | 500 | 42 | **training log only** | ⚠️ GAP |\n20\t| plan002-b03 | Additive ISR β=0.3 | r = r_exec·(1+0.3·ISR) | 500 | 42 | eval_sta.py | ✅ DONE |\n21\t| plan013-r4 | Random convex | r = 0.9·r_exec + 0.1·random | 500 | 42 | eval_sta.py | ✅ DONE |\n22\t| plan017 | Additive random β=0.3 | r = r_exec·(1+0.3·random) | 500 | 42 | eval_sta.py | ✅ DONE |\n23\t| plan014 | Downstream NLI | — | — | 42 | eval_downstream.py | ✅ DONE (negative) |\n24\t| plan002-b01 | Additive ISR β=0.1 | r = r_exec·(1+0.1·ISR) | 500 | 42 | — | 🔄 RUNNING |\n25\t| plan016 | Exec-only extended | r = r_exec | 1000 | 42 | — | 🔄 RUNNING |\n26\t\n27\t---\n28\t\n29\t## Claim 1: ISR as Reward Hacking Diagnostic\n30\t\n31\t> \"STA derives ISR via component necessity testing. ISR detects reward hacking that prove_rate alone misses.\"\n32\t\n33\t### Supporting Evidence\n34\t\n35\t| Evidence Point | Experiment | Key Metrics | Strength |\n36\t|---|---|---|---|\n37\t| Early training = structurally sound | plan003-eval-r5 | PR=32%, proved_ISR=**0.6423** | ✅ Strong (eval_sta.py) |\n38\t| Late training = structural collapse despite high PR | plan001-s42-r2 | PR=**93%**, ISR=0.1232, proved_ISR=**0.1324**, median_ISR=0 | ✅ Strong (eval_sta.py) |\n39\t| ISR collapse magnitude | plan003→plan001-s42 | proved_ISR: **0.6423 → 0.1324** (−79%) | ✅ Strong |\n40\t| Seed 43: repetition collapse | plan001-s43-r4 | PR=**14%**, ISR=0, 87% hit max_tokens | ⚠️ Medium (sampling eval, not eval_sta.py — **violates C004**) |\n41\t| Seed 44: tautological collapse | plan001-s44 | PR=**98%**, ISR=0.57 (fake-high), comp=**2.04**, 94% 2-component | ✅ Strong (eval_sta.py) |\n42\t| Base model reference | sta-phase0-baseline | PR=12%, ISR=0.0641 | ✅ Reference |\n43\t| Ground truth ISR ceiling | sta-gt-isr-baseline | GT proved_ISR=**0.5588** | ✅ Reference |\n44\t| Hacking taxonomy (5 modes) | plan012 report + plan017 D027 | Qualitative + quantitative | ✅ Strong (artifact-based) |\n45\t\n46\t### 3-Seed Summary (Exec-only 500 steps)\n47\t\n48\t| Seed | eval PR | eval ISR | eval proved_ISR | Hacking Mode |\n49\t|------|---------|----------|-----------------|--------------|\n50\t| 42 | 93% | 0.1232 | 0.1324 | Conclusion embedding |\n51\t| 43 | 14% | 0 | — | Repetition/length collapse |\n52\t| 44 | 98% | 0.57 (fake) | 0.5816 | Tautological collapse (comp=2.04) |\n53\t| **mean±std** | **68±48%** | **0.23±0.30** | — | 3 distinct modes |\n54\t\n55\t### Evidence Strength: ⭐⭐⭐⭐ (4/5)\n56\t\n57\t**Strong points:**\n58\t- ISR collapse 0.6423→0.1324 is dramatic and clean (same seed, different training steps)\n59\t- 3 seeds showing 3 different hacking modes is a powerful finding\n60\t- All from eval_sta.py except s43\n61\t\n62\t### Gaps\n63\t\n64\t1. **CRITICAL: plan001-s43-r4 uses sampling eval, not eval_sta.py.** Metrics are `eval_sampling_*` with `do_sample=True, temperature=0.7`. Per C004, cross-seed ISR comparison requires eval_sta.py. **Action needed: re-run eval_sta.py on s43 checkpoint `/root/autodl-tmp/outputs/plan001_exec_only_s43_r4`.**\n65\t2. s43 component count not available — needed for hacking mode classification.\n66\t\n67\t---\n68\t\n69\t## Claim 2: GRPO Saturation Mechanism\n70\t\n71\t> \"When prove_rate → 1.0, reward_std → 0 and loss → 0, training stalls. Adding any variance redirects but doesn't prevent hacking.\"\n72\t\n73\t### Supporting Evidence\n74\t\n75\t| Evidence Point | Experiment | Key Metrics | Strength |\n76\t|---|---|---|---|\n77\t| Exec-only saturation: PR→1, loss→0 | plan001-s42-r2 | train last100 PR=not avail from eval, but ISR collapse confirms | ✅ Strong |\n78\t| Exec-only s44: PR saturation + tautological | plan001-s44 | train last100 PR=0.9988, loss=0.000419 | ✅ Strong |\n79\t| Random convex prevents saturation but tautological | plan013-r4 | eval PR=**1.0**, ISR=0.535, **100% 2-component**, all tautological | ✅ Strong |\n80\t| Additive ISR β=0.3: prevents saturation but lowest PR | plan002-b03 | eval PR=**18%**, eval ISR=0.0257, proved_ISR=0.1427 | ✅ Strong |\n81\t| Additive random β=0.3: prevents tautological but complexity-without-utility | plan017 | eval PR=**48%**, eval ISR=0.0453, comp=**9.56**, 33% proved ISR=0 | ✅ Strong |\n82\t| Convex ISR: penalty effect | plan005-sta-low | last100 PR=77.25%, ISR/PR ratio=0.298 | ⚠️ Medium (training log only) |\n83\t| **ISR worse than matched random** | plan002-b03 vs plan017 | ISR: PR=18% vs Random: PR=**48%** (same β=0.3, same formula structure) | ✅ Strong (key finding) |\n84\t\n85\t### Reward Condition Comparison (eval_sta.py where available)\n86\t\n87\t| Condition | Formula | eval PR | eval ISR | proved_ISR | comp_mean | Hacking Mode |\n88\t|-----------|---------|---------|----------|------------|-----------|--------------|\n89\t| Exec-only s42 | r_exec | 93% | 0.1232 | 0.1324 | ~6.58 | Conclusion embedding |\n90\t| Exec-only s44 | r_exec | 98% | 0.57 | 0.5816 | 2.04 | Tautological |\n91\t| Random convex | 0.9·r_exec+0.1·rand | 100% | 0.535 | 0.535 | ~2 | Tautological (100%) |\n92\t| Additive random β=0.3 | r_exec·(1+0.3·rand) | 48% | 0.0453 | 0.0943 | 9.56 | Complexity-without-utility |\n93\t| Additive ISR β=0.3 | r_exec·(1+0.3·ISR) | 18% | 0.0257 | 0.1427 | — | Repetitive cycling |\n94\t| Convex ISR (α=0.9) | 0.9·r_exec+0.1·r_exec·ISR | ~77%* | ~0.23* | — | — | ISR-PR separation |\n95\t\n96\t*plan005 values from training log, not eval_sta.py\n97\t\n98\t### Evidence Strength: ⭐⭐⭐⭐ (4/5)\n99\t\n100\t**Strong points:**\n101\t- 5 reward conditions systematically compared\n102\t- ISR vs random (plan002-b03 vs plan017) is a clean pairwise comparison: same formula structure, same β, only ISR vs random differs → ISR actively misleading (PR 18% vs 48%)\n103\t- Multiple hacking modes documented per condition\n104\t\n105\t### Gaps\n106\t\n107\t1. **plan005-sta-low lacks eval_sta.py evaluation.** Training log ISR may use binary `_fast_fn`. **Action needed: run eval_sta.py on plan005 checkpoint `/root/autodl-tmp/outputs/plan005_sta_low_s42/checkpoint-500`.**\n108\t2. **plan002-b01 (β=0.1) still running.** Fills ISR dose-response (β=0.1 vs β=0.3). Expected completion: within hours.\n109\t3. **plan016 (1000 steps) still running.** Addresses reviewer concern \"500 steps too short.\" Expected completion: within hours.\n110\t4. **All non-exec-only conditions are single-seed (s42 only).** Multi-seed data only exists for exec-only. This limits statistical claims for Claim 2 to qualitative comparisons.\n111\t5. plan013 vs plan017 formula structure difference (convex vs multiplicative) — paper_framing already notes this constraint (D027).\n112\t\n113\t---\n114\t\n115\t## Claim 3: Cross-Logic Generality\n116\t\n117\t> \"STA protocol is solver-agnostic: hacking modes and ISR diagnostic value replicate across FOL→Prover9 and Prolog→SWI-Prolog.\"\n118\t\n119\t### Supporting Evidence\n120\t\n121\t**None.** plan006 Prolog GRPO experiment has not been started.\n122\t\n123\t### Evidence Strength: ⭐ (0/5 — no evidence)\n124\t\n125\t### Assessment\n126\t\n127\tWith 11 days to deadline, starting a full Prolog GRPO training pipeline (data prep + training + eval_sta.py adaptation + analysis) is extremely risky. **Recommendation: downgrade to Future Work.** The paper already has enough depth with FOL-only analysis (3 seeds × 5+ conditions × 5 hacking modes).\n128\t\n129\t---\n130\t\n131\t## ISR Capability Boundary (Supplementary Claim)\n132\t\n133\t> \"ISR measures syntactic component necessity, not semantic faithfulness.\"\n134\t\n135\t### Supporting Evidence\n136\t\n137\t| Evidence Point | Experiment | Key Metrics | Strength |\n138\t|---|---|---|---|\n139\t| ISR-NLI correlation null | plan014 | Spearman ρ=**−0.049** (p=0.187, NS) | ✅ Strong negative |\n140\t| Best-of-N ISR vs random | plan014 | +0.9pp (NS) | ✅ Strong negative |\n141\t| Model true-bias ceiling | plan014 | Overall accuracy=34.1%, false accuracy=0% | ✅ Explains null |\n142\t| Weak bucket-level trend | plan014 | high=75%, mid=37.7%, low=32.7% (but n=12 for high) | ⚠️ Suggestive |\n143\t\n144\t### Evidence Strength: ⭐⭐⭐⭐ (4/5 as negative result)\n145\t\n146\tWell-characterized null result with clear mechanistic explanation (true-bias). Suitable for Limitations section.\n147\t\n148\t---\n149\t\n150\t## Pending Experiments Impact\n151\t\n152\t### plan002-b01 (Additive ISR β=0.1) — RUNNING\n153\t\n154\t**Fills:** Claim 2 ISR dose-response. If β=0.1 outperforms β=0.3 (PR>18%), suggests ISR signal is useful at lower intensity. If also poor, strengthens \"ISR actively misleading\" narrative.\n155\t\n156\t**Table 1 impact:** Adds one row to reward condition comparison.\n157\t\n158\t### plan016 (Exec-only 1000 steps) — RUNNING\n159\t\n160\t**Fills:** Reviewer concern #5 (\"500 steps too short\"). Shows whether hacking stabilizes, worsens, or recovers with extended training. Also whether s42's apparent \"genuine\" proofs degrade further.\n161\t\n162\t**Table 1 impact:** Adds temporal dimension. Could show ISR trajectory figure (100→500→1000 steps).\n163\t\n164\t### plan006 (Prolog 3-seed) — NOT STARTED\n165\t\n166\t**Would fill:** Claim 3 entirely. Without it, Claim 3 = Future Work.\n167\t\n168\t**Assessment:** Not feasible in 11 days given pipeline complexity. Drop from main claims.\n169\t\n170\t---\n171\t\n172\t## Table 1 Design\n173\t\n174\t### Recommended Structure\n175\t\n176\t**Table 1: Eval metrics across reward conditions (eval_sta.py, proofwriter_fol_100)**\n177\t\n178\t| Condition | Formula | PR↑ | ISR_mean | ISR_proved | Comp_mean | Taut? | Hacking |\n179\t|-----------|---------|-----|----------|------------|-----------|-------|---------|\n180\t| Base model | — | 12% | 0.064 | — | — | — | — |\n181\t| GT FOL | — | 18% | — | 0.559 | — | — | — |\n182\t| Exec-only 100step | r_exec | 32% | 0.206 | 0.642 | — | No | — |\n183\t| Exec-only 500step s42 | r_exec | 93% | 0.123 | 0.132 | ~6.6 | No | Conclusion embed |\n184\t| Exec-only 500step s43 | r_exec | 14% | 0† | — | —† | No | Repetition |\n185\t| Exec-only 500step s44 | r_exec | 98% | 0.570 | 0.582 | 2.04 | **Yes** | Tautological |\n186\t| Exec-only **mean±std** | r_exec | **68±48%** | **0.23±0.30** | — | — | — | 3 modes |\n187\t| Convex ISR (α=0.9) | 0.9e+0.1eI | ~77%* | ~0.23* | —* | — | No | ISR-PR sep |\n188\t| Additive ISR β=0.3 | e(1+0.3I) | 18% | 0.026 | 0.143 | — | No | Cycling |\n189\t| Additive ISR β=0.1 | e(1+0.1I) | **TBD** | **TBD** | **TBD** | **TBD** | TBD | TBD |\n190\t| Random convex | 0.9e+0.1r | 100% | 0.535 | 0.535 | ~2 | **Yes** | Tautological |\n191\t| Additive random β=0.3 | e(1+0.3r) | 48% | 0.045 | 0.094 | 9.56 | No | Complexity |\n192\t\n193\t† s43 needs eval_sta.py re-evaluation  \n194\t\\* plan005 needs eval_sta.py evaluation  \n195\t**TBD** = plan002-b01 running\n196\t\n197\t### Missing Data for Table 1\n198\t\n199\t1. **plan001-s43 eval_sta.py** — currently only has sampling eval\n200\t2. **plan005 eval_sta.py** — currently only has training log metrics\n201\t3. **plan002-b01 eval** — experiment still running\n202\t4. **plan001-s42 component_count_mean** — not in registry metrics (need to extract from eval output)\n203\t5. **plan016 eval** — experiment still running\n204\t\n205\t---\n206\t\n207\t## Priority Actions (ordered by impact)\n208\t\n209\t1. **🔴 CRITICAL: Run eval_sta.py on plan001-s43-r4 checkpoint.** Without this, 3-seed comparison violates C004. The s43 ISR=0 claim is currently unsupported by standardized evaluation.\n210\t\n211\t2. **🟡 HIGH: Run eval_sta.py on plan005 checkpoint.** Convex combination is a key Claim 2 data point. Training log ISR uses binary `_fast_fn`, unreliable for paper.\n212\t\n213\t3. **🟢 WAIT: plan002-b01 and plan016 complete + auto-eval.** These are running and should auto-trigger eval on completion.\n214\t\n215\t4. **⚪ DROP: plan006 Prolog.** Insufficient time. Downgrade Claim 3 to Future Work.\n216\t\n217\t---\n218\t\n219\t## Summary\n220\t\n221\t| Claim | Evidence Status | Gaps | Rating |\n222\t|-------|----------------|------|--------|\n223\t| C1: ISR as Hacking Diagnostic | 3 seeds done, ISR collapse documented, taxonomy exists | s43 needs eval_sta.py | ⭐⭐⭐⭐ |\n224\t| C2: GRPO Saturation | 5 conditions compared, ISR<random confirmed | plan005 needs eval_sta.py; b01/016 pending | ⭐⭐⭐⭐ |\n225\t| C3: Cross-Logic Generality | No evidence | plan006 not started | ⭐ (→Future Work) |\n226\t| ISR Boundary (Limitation) | Well-characterized null | None | ⭐⭐⭐⭐ |\n227\t\n228\t**Bottom line:** Claims 1 and 2 have strong evidence with two fixable gaps (eval_sta.py for s43 and plan005). Claim 3 should be dropped to Future Work. Two running experiments (plan002-b01, plan016) will strengthen but are not critical. The paper is writable with current evidence once the two eval_sta.py gaps are filled.\n229\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01Hts9s1QZKBtk1YDsUoncb6","session_id":"cb7ceeff-4816-4704-b3bd-c692a0f9b846","uuid":"370c6c51-cbc2-4cc6-a785-5de64a2dbc51","timesta